# @imqueue — Full documentation

> {{ site.definition }} This file concatenates the framework documentation as a single markdown document for AI ingestion. Canonical HTML: {{ siteUrl }}/. Commercial licensing: https://imqueue.com/.

Roughly {{ fullKb }} KB / {{ fullTokens }}k tokens across {{ docCount }} documents (the bodies below; this header adds a little).
If that does not fit, fetch {{ siteUrl }}/llms.txt instead and follow the links —
every page listed there is also served as plain markdown at `<page-url>index.md` and
at `<page>.md` — byte-identical.
Documents appear below in reading order: orientation, then the tutorial, the CLI
manual, the MCP server and the agent recipes, then the articles, then the hand-written
API guide, with legal pages last. Each is separated by `---` and headed by a `#` title
and a `Source:` line carrying its canonical URL.

{% comment -%}
The three lead titles are written out because their documents come from includes
rather than from a page with `title` front matter. They must match the H1 each
include actually opens with — /intro/'s is site.definitionShort, not its page title,
which is why entry 2 reads the way it does. Verified by diffing these three lines
against the leading-hash lines of the built file.

Tag shapes matter here. The opening tag has NO leading dash and the closing tag NO
trailing one: a leading dash strips the newline ending the paragraph above, which
shipped "…carrying its canonical URL." glued to the heading below on one line. A
first attempt to document that quoted the tags literally inside this comment, and
LiquidJS closed the comment at the quoted end tag and printed the rest of the prose
into the file — so do not name the tags here.
